---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';

const title = 'Magazine Article Template';
const description = 'A standalone magazine-style article template with placeholder editorial content.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title={title} description={description} image="/blog-placeholder-2.jpg" />
  </head>
  <body class="article-copy">
    <header class="copy-header">
      <a class="copy-mark" href="/" aria-label="Home">*</a>
      <button class="menu-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Toggle menu" aria-expanded="false">
        <span></span>
        <span></span>
        <span></span>
      </button>
      <nav class="main-menu" aria-label="Primary">
        <div class="menu-inner">
          <a href="/" class="menu-link active">All Notes</a>
          <a href="/about/" class="menu-link">Contributors</a>
          <a href="/page-types/" class="menu-link">About</a>
          <a href="/tweets/" class="menu-link">Notes</a>
          <a href="/music/" class="menu-link">Archive</a>
          <aside class="newsletter-card">
            <form class="newsletter-form">
              <p>Sign up for essays, interviews, and notes from the desk.</p>
              <div>
                <input type="email" name="email" placeholder="Your email address" required />
                <button type="submit">Sign up</button>
              </div>
              <small class="form-status" aria-live="polite"></small>
            </form>
          </aside>
          <div class="menu-footer">
            <a href="/">Sign in</a>
            <a href="/">Privacy Policy</a>
            <span>2026</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main class="post-shell">
      <div class="progress-rail" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="progress-bar"></div>
        <div class="chapter-indicators"></div>
      </div>

      <header class="opener">
        <p class="issue-label">Issue 00 / Field Notes</p>
        <h1>Why This Article Layout Works So Well</h1>
        <p class="authors"><span>Author Name</span></p>
      </header>

      <section class="content">
        <div class="intro">
          <p>
            A precise article page needs a strong opening, steady prose rhythm, room for visual interruption,
            and enough navigational hardware to keep a long read from becoming shapeless.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="content-blocks">
          <div class="text-container">
            <div class="text">
              <p>
                The first section starts without decoration. It gives the reader a clean run of paragraphs before
                any secondary system asks for attention. Links, emphasis, footnotes, images, and newsletter modules
                all need to sit inside the article without changing the basic measure of the text.
              </p>
              <p>
                This template keeps the text column narrow enough for comfort, but the page itself remains wide.
                That extra width gives the progress rail, chapter marks, and notes a place to live.
              </p>
              <p>
                The visual language is editorial rather than dashboard-like: cream paper, black text, blue accents,
                large italic serif display type, compact sans-serif utilities, and very thin dividing rules.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="image-block">
              <figure>
                <img src="/blog-placeholder-2.jpg" alt="Abstract placeholder landscape" />
                <figcaption>
                  <small>Local placeholder image</small>
                </figcaption>
              </figure>
            </div>

            <div class="heading">
              <h2>Designing the Opener</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="text">
              <p>
                A large opener works best when it is a little wider than the body text. It makes the article feel
                like a magazine piece while keeping the actual reading column restrained.
              </p>
              <p>
                The author line inherits the same display type as the headline, which makes the byline part of the
                opening composition instead of a small metadata afterthought.
              </p>
              <p>
                In the reference pattern, section headings also become waypoints. This copy builds markers from the
                second-level headings and places them on the left rail after the reader begins scrolling.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="heading">
              <h2>Notes and Margins</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="text">
              <p>
                Footnotes can be more useful when they appear beside the relevant line on wide screens. On smaller
                screens, the same notes become tap-to-open popovers so they do not break the reading flow
                <sup class="footnote"><a href="#fn-1" id="fnref-1">1</a></sup>.
              </p>
              <p>
                The note rail is positioned relative to the content area, not the viewport. That keeps each note near
                the reference that summoned it and avoids a separate endnotes-only experience.
              </p>
              <p>
                External links can be marked in script, progress can be updated on scroll, and the layout still
                degrades to a readable article if JavaScript is unavailable.
              </p>
            </div>

            <aside class="newsletter-card padded">
              <form class="newsletter-form">
                <p>Get the next article when it is published.</p>
                <div>
                  <input type="email" name="email" placeholder="Your email address" required />
                  <button type="submit">Sign up</button>
                </div>
                <small class="form-status" aria-live="polite"></small>
              </form>
            </aside>

            <div class="heading">
              <h2>Interruptions That Hold Shape</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="text">
              <p>
                Long essays benefit from deliberate interruptions. A figure, a pull quote, a subscription module,
                or a ruled list can reset attention without turning the page into a stack of cards.
              </p>
              <blockquote>
                <p>A good article layout gives the reader landmarks without shouting over the prose.</p>
              </blockquote>
              <p>
                The surrounding whitespace does most of the work. Every module returns to the same text width, so the
                reader never has to relearn where the article lives.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="heading">
              <h2>Footer Systems</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="text">
              <p>
                The bottom of the article gathers everything that would be distracting at the top: author biography,
                publication date, previous and next links, tags, and a compact list of related articles.
              </p>
              <p>
                The related rows are intentionally plain. Thin borders, mixed title weights, and right-aligned authors
                are enough to make the list scannable without turning it into a visual gallery
                <sup class="footnote"><a href="#fn-2" id="fnref-2">2</a></sup>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="notes-container" aria-label="Footnotes">
            <ol class="footnotes-list">
              <li id="fn-1">
                Wide-screen notes are placed alongside the paragraph that references them. On mobile, tapping the
                number opens this note as a small overlay.
                <button type="button" class="close-note" aria-label="Close footnote">x</button>
              </li>
              <li id="fn-2">
                This related-list treatment is structural only. Replace every title and author with real article
                data when adapting the template.
                <button type="button" class="close-note" aria-label="Close footnote">x</button>
              </li>
            </ol>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <footer class="article-footer">
        <ul class="author-list">
          <li>
            <p>
              <strong>Author Name</strong> writes essays about interfaces, archives, reading systems, and the
              small decisions that make long documents easier to finish.
            </p>
            <ul class="author-articles">
              <li><a href="/">Earlier Essay, Issue 00</a></li>
              <li><a href="/">Another Article, Issue 00</a></li>
            </ul>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <aside class="newsletter-card padded">
          <form class="newsletter-form">
            <p>Sign up for future essays and project notes.</p>
            <div>
              <input type="email" name="email" placeholder="Your email address" required />
              <button type="submit">Sign up</button>
            </div>
            <small class="form-status" aria-live="polite"></small>
          </form>
        </aside>

        <p class="published">Published <time datetime="2026-06">June 2026</time></p>
        <p>Have something to say? Email <a href="mailto:hello@example.com">hello@example.com</a>.</p>
      </footer>

      <section class="prev-next" aria-label="Previous and next articles">
        <div>
          <a href="/"><strong>Previous</strong><br />A Compact Archive Page</a>
        </div>
        <div>
          <a href="/"><strong>Next</strong><br />A Better Reading Queue</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="see-also">
        <h2>See also</h2>
        <div class="article-tags" aria-label="Tags">
          <span>design</span>
          <span>reading</span>
          <span>systems</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="related">
          <li>
            <h3 class="sans italic"><a href="/">How to Lay Out a Long Note</a></h3>
            <p>Editor One</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3><a href="/">Small Type, Big Pages</a></h3>
            <p>Editor Two</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3><a href="/">The Work of Margins</a></h3>
            <p>Editor Three</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3 class="sans"><a href="/">A Quiet Table of Contents</a></h3>
            <p>Editor Four</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </main>

    <style is:global>
      body.article-copy {
        --copy-black: #070707;
        --copy-blue: #2f95d4;
        --copy-blue-soft: #b7d9ec;
        --copy-cream: #fbfaf3;
        --copy-rule: #111;
        --copy-muted: #6c6b66;
        --copy-text-width: 750px;
        --copy-pad: 32px;
        --copy-pad-lg: 80px;
        --copy-display: CopyArticleDisplay, Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
        --copy-serif: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
        --copy-sans: Atkinson, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
        margin: 0;
        background: var(--copy-cream);
        color: var(--copy-black);
        font-family: var(--copy-serif);
        font-size: 18px;
      }

      @font-face {
        font-family: CopyArticleDisplay;
        src: url('/fonts/DEMO-caslongrad.otf') format('opentype');
        font-weight: 400 700;
        font-style: normal;
        font-display: swap;
      }

      body.article-copy a {
        color: inherit;
        text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
        text-underline-offset: 0.16em;
      }

      body.article-copy .copy-header {
        position: absolute;
        top: 0;
        left: 0;
        z-index: 80;
        min-height: 62px;
        padding: 8px var(--copy-pad);
        font-family: var(--copy-sans);
      }

      body.article-copy .copy-mark {
        display: inline-flex;
        width: 42px;
        height: 42px;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        color: var(--copy-blue);
        font-family: var(--copy-display);
        font-size: 52px;
        font-weight: 700;
        line-height: 1;
        text-decoration: none;
        opacity: 0.84;
      }

      body.article-copy .menu-toggle {
        position: fixed;
        top: 16px;
        right: 18px;
        z-index: 120;
        display: grid;
        gap: 5px;
        width: 42px;
        height: 42px;
        padding: 10px;
        border: 1px solid rgba(7, 7, 7, 0.32);
        border-radius: 0;
        background: rgba(251, 250, 243, 0.84);
        cursor: pointer;
      }

      body.article-copy .menu-toggle span {
        display: block;
        height: 2px;
        background: var(--copy-black);
      }

      body.article-copy .main-menu {
        position: fixed;
        inset: 0;
        z-index: 100;
        display: none;
        background: rgba(250, 248, 240, 0.98);
      }

      body.article-copy.menu-open .main-menu {
        display: block;
      }

      body.article-copy .menu-inner {
        width: min(460px, calc(100vw - 40px));
        min-height: 100%;
        padding: 72px 24px 24px;
        border-right: 1px solid var(--copy-rule);
        background: var(--copy-cream);
      }

      body.article-copy .menu-link {
        display: block;
        padding: 0.08em 0;
        font-size: clamp(34px, 6vw, 70px);
        font-weight: 700;
        line-height: 0.95;
        text-decoration: none;
      }

      body.article-copy .menu-link.active,
      body.article-copy .menu-link:hover {
        color: var(--copy-blue);
      }

      body.article-copy .menu-footer {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 12px;
        margin-top: 28px;
        font-size: 13px;
      }

      body.article-copy .post-shell {
        position: relative;
        padding: 0 var(--copy-pad) 80px;
      }

      body.article-copy .opener {
        width: min(920px, calc(100vw - 2 * var(--copy-pad)));
        margin: 0 auto 42px;
        padding-top: 4px;
        color: var(--copy-blue);
      }

      body.article-copy .issue-label {
        margin: 0 0 10px;
        font-family: var(--copy-sans);
        font-size: 13px;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        opacity: 0;
        pointer-events: none;
      }

      body.article-copy h1 {
        max-width: 1030px;
        margin: 0;
        font-family: var(--copy-display);
        font-size: clamp(58px, 8.2vw, 112px);
        font-style: italic;
        font-weight: 600;
        line-height: 0.9;
        letter-spacing: 0;
      }

      body.article-copy .authors {
        margin: 10px 0 0;
        font-family: var(--copy-display);
        font-size: clamp(48px, 6.7vw, 96px);
        font-weight: 400;
        line-height: 0.92;
        letter-spacing: 0;
      }

      body.article-copy .content {
        position: relative;
      }

      body.article-copy .intro,
      body.article-copy .text p,
      body.article-copy .heading h2,
      body.article-copy blockquote,
      body.article-copy .newsletter-card,
      body.article-copy .image-block figure {
        width: min(var(--copy-text-width), calc(100vw - 2 * var(--copy-pad)));
        margin-left: auto;
        margin-right: auto;
      }

      body.article-copy .intro {
        margin-bottom: 42px;
        color: var(--copy-blue);
        font-family: var(--copy-display);
        font-size: clamp(30px, 3.55vw, 39px);
        font-weight: 400;
        line-height: 1.08;
        letter-spacing: 0;
      }

      body.article-copy .intro p {
        margin: 0;
      }

      body.article-copy .content-blocks {
        position: relative;
      }

      body.article-copy .text p {
        margin-top: 0;
        margin-bottom: 1.28em;
        font-size: 20px;
        font-weight: 700;
        line-height: 1.34;
        font-feature-settings: "onum" 1;
      }

      body.article-copy .heading h2 {
        margin-top: 2.4em;
        margin-bottom: 0.7em;
        color: var(--copy-blue);
        font-family: var(--copy-display);
        font-size: clamp(34px, 4vw, 50px);
        font-weight: 400;
        line-height: 1.12;
      }

      body.article-copy .image-block {
        padding: 24px 0 10px;
      }

      body.article-copy .image-block img {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
        aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
        object-fit: cover;
        filter: saturate(0.85) contrast(1.04);
      }

      body.article-copy figcaption {
        margin-top: 8px;
        font-family: var(--copy-sans);
        font-size: 12px;
        color: var(--copy-muted);
      }

      body.article-copy blockquote {
        box-sizing: border-box;
        margin-top: 28px;
        margin-bottom: 28px;
        padding: 0 32px;
        border-left: 1px solid var(--copy-rule);
        color: var(--copy-blue);
        font-family: var(--copy-display);
        font-size: clamp(26px, 3vw, 38px);
        line-height: 1.16;
      }

      body.article-copy blockquote p {
        margin: 0;
      }

      body.article-copy .newsletter-card {
        box-sizing: border-box;
        margin-top: 34px;
        margin-bottom: 34px;
        padding: 18px 0;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--copy-rule);
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--copy-rule);
        font-family: var(--copy-sans);
      }

      body.article-copy .newsletter-card p {
        margin: 0 0 12px;
        font-size: 15px;
        font-weight: 600;
        line-height: 1.35;
      }

      body.article-copy .newsletter-form div {
        display: flex;
        border: 1px solid var(--copy-rule);
      }

      body.article-copy .newsletter-form input {
        min-width: 0;
        flex: 1;
        border: 0;
        border-radius: 0;
        padding: 12px;
        background: var(--copy-cream);
        color: var(--copy-black);
        font: inherit;
      }

      body.article-copy .newsletter-form button {
        border: 0;
        border-left: 1px solid var(--copy-rule);
        border-radius: 0;
        padding: 0 16px;
        background: var(--copy-blue);
        color: white;
        font: inherit;
        font-weight: 700;
        cursor: pointer;
      }

      body.article-copy .form-status {
        display: block;
        min-height: 1.2em;
        margin-top: 8px;
        color: var(--copy-blue);
        font-size: 12px;
      }

      body.article-copy sup.footnote {
        font-family: var(--copy-sans);
        font-size: 0.62em;
        font-weight: 700;
        color: var(--copy-blue);
      }

      body.article-copy sup.footnote a {
        text-decoration: none;
      }

      body.article-copy .notes-container {
        position: absolute;
        top: 0;
        left: calc(50vw + var(--copy-text-width) / 2 + 32px);
        width: min(280px, calc(50vw - var(--copy-text-width) / 2 - 64px));
      }

      body.article-copy .footnotes-list {
        margin: 0;
        padding-left: 20px;
      }

      body.article-copy .footnotes-list li {
        position: absolute;
        opacity: 0;
        font-family: var(--copy-sans);
        font-size: 12px;
        line-height: 1.42;
        transition: opacity 0.2s ease;
      }

      body.article-copy .footnotes-list li::marker {
        color: var(--copy-blue);
        font-weight: 700;
      }

      body.article-copy .close-note {
        display: none;
      }

      body.article-copy .article-footer,
      body.article-copy .prev-next,
      body.article-copy .see-also {
        width: min(var(--copy-text-width), calc(100vw - 2 * var(--copy-pad)));
        margin-left: auto;
        margin-right: auto;
        font-family: var(--copy-sans);
        font-size: 14px;
        line-height: 1.5;
      }

      body.article-copy .article-footer {
        margin-top: 42px;
        padding: 28px 0;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--copy-rule);
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--copy-rule);
      }

      body.article-copy .author-list,
      body.article-copy .author-articles,
      body.article-copy .related {
        list-style: none;
        padding: 0;
      }

      body.article-copy .author-list,
      body.article-copy .author-list p,
      body.article-copy .published {
        margin: 0 0 12px;
      }

      body.article-copy .author-articles {
        margin: 0 0 22px;
      }

      body.article-copy .author-articles li {
        display: inline;
        margin-right: 12px;
      }

      body.article-copy .author-articles li::before {
        content: "-> ";
        color: var(--copy-blue);
      }

      body.article-copy .prev-next {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
        gap: 28px;
        margin-top: 32px;
        margin-bottom: 36px;
      }

      body.article-copy .prev-next div:last-child {
        text-align: right;
      }

      body.article-copy .prev-next a {
        text-decoration: none;
      }

      body.article-copy .see-also h2 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 14px;
        text-transform: uppercase;
      }

      body.article-copy .article-tags {
        margin-bottom: 16px;
        font-weight: 700;
      }

      body.article-copy .article-tags span:not(:last-child)::after {
        content: ", ";
      }

      body.article-copy .related {
        margin: 0;
      }

      body.article-copy .related li {
        position: relative;
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr;
        gap: 18px;
        align-items: center;
        padding: 12px 0;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--copy-rule);
      }

      body.article-copy .related li:last-child {
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--copy-rule);
      }

      body.article-copy .related li:hover {
        color: var(--copy-blue);
      }

      body.article-copy .related h3 {
        margin: 0;
        font-family: var(--copy-display);
        font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 42px);
        line-height: 1;
      }

      body.article-copy .related h3.sans {
        font-family: var(--copy-sans);
        letter-spacing: 0;
      }

      body.article-copy .related h3.italic {
        font-style: italic;
      }

      body.article-copy .related a {
        text-decoration: none;
      }

      body.article-copy .related a::after {
        content: "";
        position: absolute;
        inset: 0;
      }

      body.article-copy .related p {
        margin: 0;
        text-align: right;
      }

      body.article-copy .progress-bar {
        position: fixed;
        top: 0;
        left: 0;
        z-index: 70;
        width: 32px;
        height: 0;
        background: var(--copy-blue);
        opacity: 0;
        transition: opacity 0.15s ease;
      }

      body.article-copy .chapter-indicators a {
        position: fixed;
        left: 0;
        z-index: 71;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        width: min(340px, 28vw);
        color: var(--copy-black);
        font-family: var(--copy-sans);
        font-size: 12px;
        text-decoration: none;
        transform: translateX(-100%);
        transition: transform 0.2s ease;
      }

      body.article-copy .chapter-indicators .dot {
        width: 46px;
        height: 12px;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--copy-black);
      }

      body.article-copy .chapter-indicators .label {
        opacity: 0;
        margin-left: 8px;
        transition: opacity 0.2s ease;
      }

      body.article-copy.progress-visible .progress-bar {
        opacity: 1;
      }

      body.article-copy.progress-visible .chapter-indicators a {
        transform: translateX(0);
      }

      body.article-copy .chapter-indicators a:hover .label {
        opacity: 1;
      }

      @media (max-width: 1300px) {
        body.article-copy {
          --copy-text-width: 58vw;
        }

        body.article-copy .opener {
          width: min(860px, calc(100vw - 2 * var(--copy-pad)));
        }
      }

      @media (max-width: 1024px) {
        body.article-copy {
          --copy-text-width: 64vw;
        }

        body.article-copy .notes-container {
          left: 0;
          width: 100%;
          max-width: none;
        }

        body.article-copy .footnotes-list li {
          display: none;
          position: fixed;
          left: 20px !important;
          right: 20px;
          bottom: 20px;
          top: auto !important;
          z-index: 130;
          box-sizing: border-box;
          width: auto;
          max-width: 560px;
          padding: 18px 44px 18px 22px;
          border: 1px solid var(--copy-rule);
          background: var(--copy-cream);
          box-shadow: 0 12px 28px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.14);
          opacity: 1;
        }

        body.article-copy .footnotes-list li.show {
          display: block;
        }

        body.article-copy .close-note {
          position: absolute;
          top: 8px;
          right: 10px;
          display: block;
          border: 0;
          background: transparent;
          color: var(--copy-blue);
          font-family: var(--copy-sans);
          font-size: 18px;
          font-weight: 700;
          cursor: pointer;
        }
      }

      @media (max-width: 768px) {
        body.article-copy {
          --copy-pad: 20px;
          --copy-text-width: none;
          font-size: 17px;
        }

        body.article-copy .post-shell {
          padding-top: 0;
        }

        body.article-copy .menu-inner {
          width: 100%;
          border-right: 0;
        }

        body.article-copy .opener {
          margin-top: 4px;
        }

        body.article-copy .newsletter-form div {
          display: block;
        }

        body.article-copy .newsletter-form input,
        body.article-copy .newsletter-form button {
          box-sizing: border-box;
          width: 100%;
        }

        body.article-copy .newsletter-form button {
          border-top: 1px solid var(--copy-rule);
          border-left: 0;
          padding: 12px;
        }

        body.article-copy .progress-bar {
          width: 10px;
        }

        body.article-copy .chapter-indicators {
          display: none;
        }

        body.article-copy .prev-next,
        body.article-copy .related li {
          grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        }

        body.article-copy .prev-next div:last-child,
        body.article-copy .related p {
          text-align: left;
        }
      }
    </style>

    <script>
      const body = document.body;
      const menuToggle = document.querySelector('.menu-toggle');
      const progressBar = document.querySelector('.progress-bar');
      const chapterIndicators = document.querySelector('.chapter-indicators');
      const content = document.querySelector('.content');
      const contentBlocks = document.querySelector('.content-blocks');
      const footnoteLinks = [...document.querySelectorAll('sup.footnote a[href^="#fn-"]')];
      const footnotes = new Map(
        [...document.querySelectorAll('.footnotes-list li[id^="fn-"]')].map((note) => [note.id, note])
      );
      const mobileMq = window.matchMedia('(max-width: 1024px)');

      menuToggle?.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const isOpen = body.classList.toggle('menu-open');
        menuToggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(isOpen));
      });

      document.querySelectorAll('.newsletter-form').forEach((form) => {
        form.addEventListener('submit', (event) => {
          event.preventDefault();
          const status = form.querySelector('.form-status');
          if (status) status.textContent = 'Signed up locally for this template.';
          form.reset();
        });
      });

      const slugify = (text) =>
        text
          .toString()
          .normalize('NFKD')
          .toLowerCase()
          .trim()
          .replace(/\s+/g, '-')
          .replace(/[^\w-]+/g, '')
          .replace(/-+/g, '-');

      const elementProgress = (element) => {
        const pageHeight = document.documentElement.scrollHeight - window.innerHeight;
        const offsetTop = element.getBoundingClientRect().top + window.scrollY;
        return pageHeight > 0 ? (offsetTop / pageHeight) * 100 : 0;
      };

      const buildChapterMarkers = () => {
        if (!chapterIndicators || !content) return;
        chapterIndicators.innerHTML = '';

        content.querySelectorAll('h2').forEach((heading) => {
          if (!heading.id) heading.id = slugify(heading.textContent || '');

          const link = document.createElement('a');
          link.href = `#${heading.id}`;
          link.style.top = `${elementProgress(heading)}%`;
          link.innerHTML = `<span class="dot"></span><span class="label">${heading.textContent}</span>`;
          chapterIndicators.appendChild(link);
        });
      };

      const closeFootnotes = () => {
        footnotes.forEach((note) => note.classList.remove('show'));
      };

      const positionFootnotes = () => {
        if (!contentBlocks || mobileMq.matches) return;
        const contentTop = contentBlocks.getBoundingClientRect().top + window.scrollY;
        let previousBottom = 0;

        footnoteLinks.forEach((link) => {
          const note = footnotes.get(link.hash.slice(1));
          if (!note) return;

          let top = link.getBoundingClientRect().top + window.scrollY - contentTop;
          if (top < previousBottom) top = previousBottom + 16;
          note.style.top = `${top}px`;
          note.style.opacity = '1';
          previousBottom = top + note.getBoundingClientRect().height;
        });
      };

      footnoteLinks.forEach((link) => {
        link.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
          if (!mobileMq.matches) return;
          event.preventDefault();
          closeFootnotes();
          footnotes.get(link.hash.slice(1))?.classList.add('show');
        });
      });

      document.querySelectorAll('.close-note').forEach((button) => {
        button.addEventListener('click', () => closeFootnotes());
      });

      contentBlocks?.querySelectorAll('a[href]').forEach((link) => {
        try {
          const url = new URL(link.href, window.location.origin);
          if (url.hostname !== window.location.hostname) {
            link.target = '_blank';
            link.rel = 'noreferrer noopener';
          }
        } catch {
          // Ignore malformed hrefs.
        }
      });

      let ticking = false;
      const updateProgress = () => {
        if (ticking) return;
        ticking = true;

        requestAnimationFrame(() => {
          const pageHeight = document.documentElement.scrollHeight - window.innerHeight;
          const percent = pageHeight > 0 ? (window.scrollY / pageHeight) * 100 : 0;
          if (progressBar) progressBar.style.height = `${percent}%`;
          body.classList.toggle('progress-visible', window.scrollY > 300);
          ticking = false;
        });
      };

      const refreshLayout = () => {
        buildChapterMarkers();
        positionFootnotes();
        updateProgress();
      };

      window.addEventListener('scroll', updateProgress, { passive: true });
      window.addEventListener('resize', refreshLayout);
      mobileMq.addEventListener('change', () => {
        closeFootnotes();
        refreshLayout();
      });
      window.addEventListener('load', refreshLayout);
      refreshLayout();
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
